  "caveats": [
    "The private active-context reader requires exact owner, ROOT, original journal PROMISE/BASIS, complete retained source and generation/coverage/ancestry. Candidate-only or raw caller bytes cannot mint stored proof or new voter observations.",
    "Eight actual public-bootstrap histories cover 3-voter EMPTY ACCEPT/PROOF/CERTIFICATE plus CERTIFICATE at stable sizes 3/4/5 with EMPTY and backup sources. Tests explicitly drive elections and publication; this is not autonomous membership or public READY.",
    "The process gate uses one actual 3-voter EMPTY CERTIFICATE history at 11 original context installation/cleanup boundaries, each under halt and SIGKILL, repeated recovery death, then completion. It does not establish power-loss durability or the complete distributed matrix.",
    "Independent readers first reconstruct complete original storage and exact phases, then decode actual core backup images and check document/sequence results. All originals must pass before intended mutations; normal, optimized and relocated replays must agree.",
    "Earlier failed and intermediate source snapshots/logs remain retained. The final nine Java suites run together on one immutable build; earlier partial passes are not counted as final qualification.",
    "Autonomous discovery/election scheduling, complete network ownership integration, learner ADD/REPLACE and joint completion, generalized distributed publication and the complete Phase 3 audit remain open.",
    "No public factory, persistent format, resource/deadline limit, POM, workflow, V5.2 Runner, paid experiment, push or release change."
  ],
